1. COMMANDER DECISION

I, Human Commander, hereby issue this decision establishing the intended general delegation model for Rallyproof development campaigns.

THIS IS AN ISSUED COMMANDER DECISION.

It is not a proposal, consultation draft or request for further substantive Commander approval.

The decision is final as to Commander intent and approved delegation policy.

Its operational exercise remains subject to applicable authority-establishment, independent qualification, prospective effectivity and action-time requirements.

No agent shall confuse the absence of operational effectivity with the absence of a Commander decision.

No repeated substantive Commander approval is required merely to confirm the intent already established by this order.

⸻

2. COMMANDER INTENT

Rallyproof shall operate as a professional, efficient and independently functioning AI organization.

Human Commander establishes missions, objectives, authority boundaries and reserved decisions.

Competent delegated functions shall subsequently identify, admit, prioritize, execute, review and integrate ordinary work within those boundaries.

An effectively authorized campaign should normally be capable of completing its ordinary development lifecycle, from task admission through authorized integration into main, without repeated Commander decisions.

The purpose is to eliminate unnecessary administrative friction while preserving legitimate authority, traceability, security and independent controls.

⸻

3. CORE OPERATING PRINCIPLE

ONE CAMPAIGN APPROVAL — CONTINUOUS DELEGATED EXECUTION

Once a campaign has been competently approved and made effective, authorized campaign functions shall be permitted, within their effective authority, to:

1. Identify development needs.
2. Create and prioritize subordinate tasks.
3. Admit ordinary tasks within the campaign mandate.
4. Plan and execute authorized work.
5. Create and update pull requests.
6. Conduct required testing and validation.
7. Obtain mandatory independent review.
8. Qualify changes for integration.
9. Perform authorized protected merges into main.
10. Independently verify and document completed integration.

A new Commander decision shall not be required solely because an ordinary task or development stage follows a previously approved stage.

The controlling question is whether the specific action is covered by effective delegated authority.

⸻

4. RELATIONSHIP TO EXISTING GOVERNANCE

This decision shall be implemented through Rallyproof’s existing authority structure.

The following remain applicable:

* Effective Standing Grants A/B.
* Competently established Grant C authorities.
* Effective Commander-approved campaign mandates.
* Existing section and professional authority.
* Effective global AI professional execution simplifications.
* Build Hold restrictions and qualified exceptions.
